{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Where the 0.13.0 MCP release stands\n\nRelease ticket: hyperbolic-pernicious-drongo (c066-c496-7012-4a39), in_progress. It had NO dependencies at the start of this session -- nothing connected it to any MCP work, so \"ship MCP stable\" had no defined done. Five package-level blockers are now linked `blocks` it:\n\n  dbca-97ac-ad96-4d6d  CLOSED certified   MCP LLM-tier error classification\n  e1d9-4c8e-3fd1-41c2  in_progress        /health cannot see the request path -- code MERGED (2362)\n  494b-2dd3-e9d3-4fb0  in_progress        list_tickets can close the transport -- code MERGED (2355)\n  505d-b2c5-734f-47d9  in_progress        claim gate FAILS OPEN on unresolvable ref -- code MERGED (2357)\n  aefe-614a-2631-4117  in_progress        reads return [] for a broken store -- BLOCKED, see below\n\nFOUR of five have merged code. They remain in_progress because their acceptance criteria are not yet evidenced and ticked. That gap -- code lands, ticket never closes -- was the most common failure this session: a sweep found SIX in_progress tickets whose fix was already on main and which nobody had closed, three merged days earlier.\n\n## Framing that should survive\n\n0.13.0 ships a PyPI package. \"MCP stable\" splits into (a) the package users install and (b) our on-box deployment. Most incident work here -- review-bot 502, nginx edge, terraform, Jira credentials, disk reclaim -- is (b) and does NOT block the tag. Treating every live alarm as release-critical wasted effort early.\n\n## Operator decision recorded\n\nCertification environment is NOT a gate. Any certification is as good as any other now; restricting to a trusted set is a FUTURE feature. Implemented in 2361 (MERGED): verify_opcert_record no longer refuses on principal mismatch; trust root picked strongest-first (own_key -> pinned_environment -> envelope_key), surfaced as a typed trust_basis field. Under verify.require_environment the envelope_key fallback is WITHHELD, so enforcement binds to the pinned key, never to a key the cert supplies about itself. Settles item (a) of ADR ticket 987c-67d0-258e-4069.\n\n## Highest-value open findings\n\n1. aefe (P1) -- THE APPROVED PLAN IS WRONG; redesign before anything lands. materialize_tickets builds the pinned ticket store as a BARE TREE with no .git, so a .git-less tracker dir is BOTH the poisoned production volume AND a legitimate gate snapshot. The approved .git-presence predicate rejects both, making every pinned ticket read by plan-review and completion-verifier raise store_uninitialized -- a P1 regression from a P1 fix. Full-suite proof: 6 failed / 17843 passed. A parallel session has the same defective predicate at ~/fix-rapt-read-semantics.\n2. 9d40-1db8-1bcc-4f91 (P1) -- review-bot zombie. A compose recreate SIGTERMs the bot; uvicorn closes its LISTENING SOCKET at the start of graceful shutdown, then lifespan shutdown never returns because in-flight reviews keep running. Container reports Up, worker keeps voting ~18 min, nothing bound to port 8000. Dispatch died 22 minutes and, since the Gerrit webhooks plugin is not at-least-once (ADR 0009), events in that window were DROPPED. Silent by construction. The shipped MCP server is NOT vulnerable: drain_then_exit is bounded by grace_seconds (verified).\n3. 1d1b-a719-b675-4a1f (P2) -- infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template is in NONE of autodeploy's six path manifests, so edge config is outside change detection and fails SILENTLY. a61d's merged fix cannot go live by itself.\n4. eb67-b96c-dcf0-4f86 (P1) -- terraform state holds 23 real secrets in cleartext. CONTAINED: S3 rebar-tfstate-896586841071, SSE-S3, no bucket policy, EC2 role gets implicitDeny, only the admin IAM user allowed -- a box compromise does not yield state. NOT contained: 149 retained object versions, so rotating a secret does not remove it from history.\n5. 5caa-4b63-7ea2-4e71 -- pinning uv (2367, MERGED) removed only ONE of two manifest consumers. setup-uv also calls getArtifact(...manifestUrl) UNCONDITIONALLY for the download URL and a hosted runner always reaches it, so the fetch-failed mode is NOT eliminated. The original ticket's acceptance criterion was unachievable as written.\n\n## CI reliability -- there were no flakes\n\nEvery Verified -1 investigated was deterministic:\n  2359 -- gitutil.py 833 vs the 800 cap, identical on all four platforms\n  2360 / 2362 -- broad `except Exception` on the MCP boot path without the required RemovedInputError guard\n  2361 -- types.py stale; a hand-edited GENERATED file had WIDENED trust_basis from the schema Literal to str\n  2345 -- a real test failure\nTwo failures were mislabelled \"environmental\" by misreading the workflow ECHOING ITS OWN SCRIPT SOURCE as error output. Tell: genuine failures are ##[error] lines WITHOUT the 36;1m colour prefix.\n\n## The recurring defect class -- including in this session's own work\n\nChecks that cannot distinguish the states they are meant to separate:\n  - watcher condition `grep -qE \"^(FAILED|ERROR)\"` can NEVER fire (ANSI codes precede the word); five loops leaked\n  - `gh run view --job=N --log` returns an EMPTY log while the parent run is in progress -> 0/0/0 on all greps\n  - duplicate-detection grep whose PREFIX matched two genuinely distinct historical entries\n  - idempotency check using `git diff` against HEAD, which reports drift regardless\n  - scope detector matching `^def ` but not `async def`, naming the wrong enclosing function\nAnchor every check on a known-present positive BEFORE asserting the property.\n\n## Process hazards for the next session\n\n- ANOTHER SESSION pushes under the same RebarBotNava identity. Duplicate changes on e127 (2347 vs 2351) and 6bf1 (2344 vs 2352); two sessions wrote into ONE worktree (~/rebar-wt-e127), one amending the other's uncommitted work. Check a change's rebar-ticket trailer before assuming it is yours.\n- REBASE BY current_revision, never a hardcoded patchset ref. Rebasing 2355 from refs/changes/55/2355/1 silently discarded fixture fixes already pushed in response to a CI failure.\n- CHANGELOG.md is a live conflict hotspot: every merge invalidates every other in-flight change touching it, and rebasing DROPS both votes.\n- _mcp_health.py ~777/800 and is where boot-path work lands; gitutil.py landed at 798/800 (split filed as f802-536b-0081-432a).\n- For bugfix-size-attestation the remedy is a TICKET action plus rerun-llm-review -- NOT amend+push, which trips changekind:NO_CODE_CHANGE and carries the -1 forward unreviewed.\n\n## Unreconciled, flagged not hidden\n\nOn 879b, `verify-signature --kind plan-review` reports certified while `review-plan --status` reports stale-code naming three file_impact deps -- even when passed --ref at the exact SHA the attestation was signed against. The two views disagree; not reconciled. Recorded on Gerrit 2360."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787976724107151001,"uuid":"707678da-9d99-4c8a-ae4f-680b89337ec4"}